 years ago","descriptionSource":null},"reviews":[],"comments":[{"id":22957,"parentId":null,"materialId":482013,"userId":65074,"content":"<p>all of my test tiles came out blue, no clue why. I followed the recipe to the T. Any thoughts?<\/p>","contentSource":"all of my test tiles came out blue, no clue why. I followed the recipe to the T. Any thoughts? ","cdnId":"\/materialcomments\/13\/l_482013.667dbad0e5a5c.jpg","user":{"id":65074,"name":"Matthew","description":null,"isPatron":false,"isAlchemist":false,"createdAt":"2024-06-12T03:25:26Z","updatedAt":"2026-07-21T16:02:14Z"},"createdAt":"2024-06-27T19:17:37Z","createdAtDiff":"2 years ago","updatedAt":"2024-06-27T19:17:37Z","updatedAtDiff":"2 years ago"},{"id":22960,"parentId":22957,"materialId":482013,"userId":1869,"content":"<p>Matthew\u2026 well, it is supposed to be a blue glaze \ud83d\ude09 but it does seem your glaze contains a wee bit more cobalt. Perhaps your scale doesn\u2019t quite have 0.1g or 0.01g accuracy, which would make it hard to measure 1 gram\u2026 though I would just try a bit less cobalt or cobalt carbonate instead.<br \/>\nTo properly identify the difference I would need a lot more information to be honest (particularly regarding your location and available materials, your scale, and what clays you used)<br \/>\nThat said, I do actually LOVE your results \ud83e\udd29 Feel free to add it to the pictures for this recipe.<\/p>","contentSource":"Matthew\u2026 well, it is supposed to be a blue glaze \ud83d\ude09 but it does seem your glaze contains a wee bit more cobalt. Perhaps your scale doesn\u2019t quite have 0.1g or 0.01g accuracy, which would make it hard to measure 1 gram\u2026 though I would just try a bit less cobalt or cobalt carbonate instead. \r\nTo properly identify the difference I would need a lot more information to be honest (particularly regarding your location and available materials, your scale, and what clays you used)\r\nThat said, I do actually LOVE your results \ud83e\udd29 Feel free to add it to the pictures for this recipe. ","user":{"id":1869,"name":"Ronald Boersen","description":null,"username":"ronaldboersen","cdnId":"\/profiles\/34\/l_5034.609de2247ff7f.jpg","countryId":null,"countryName":null,"url":"ronaldboersen.com","pinterest":null,"facebook":"ronald.boersen","instagram":"ronaldboersen","artaxis":null,"paypal":"https:\/\/www.paypal.com\/ncp\/payment\/ZVFLRPNHX24QQ","title":"I'm a potter, ceramic artist, glaze nerd, and educator, exploring the materiality of clay \u2014 freezing a moment in fire.","location":null,"isPatron":true,"isAlchemist":true,"createdAt":"2016-11-03T13:31:14Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-09T12:47:53Z"},"createdAt":"2024-06-28T03:27:58Z","createdAtDiff":"2 years ago","updatedAt":"2024-06-28T03:27:58Z","updatedAtDiff":"2 years ago"},{"id":23099,"parentId":22957,"materialId":482013,"userId":65074,"content":"<p>Ronald Boersen, ahhh, hahah okay thank you very much. That could be the answer. I'll run another test!<\/p>\n<p>Thanks for getting back to me :)<\/p>","contentSource":"Ronald Boersen, ahhh, hahah okay thank you very much. That could be the answer. I'll run another test! \n\nThanks for getting back to me :)","user":{"id":65074,"name":"Matthew","description":null,"isPatron":false,"isAlchemist":false,"createdAt":"2024-06-12T03:25:26Z","updatedAt":"2026-07-21T16:02:14Z"},"createdAt":"2024-07-12T19:10:45Z","createdAtDiff":"2 years ago","updatedAt":"2024-07-12T19:10:45Z","updatedAtDiff":"2 years ago"}],"translations":[{"id":1511295,"name":"DCP (NZ) - B1","other_names":null,"description":"<p>Survived the basic leach test in acid well.<\/p>","descriptionSource":"<p>Survived the basic leach test in acid well.<\/p>","locale":"en"}],"user":{"id":1869,"name":"Ronald Boersen","description":null,"username":"ronaldboersen","cdnId":"\/profiles\/34\/l_5034.609de2247ff7f.jpg","countryId":null,"countryName":null,"url":"ronaldboersen.com","pinterest":null,"facebook":"ronald.boersen","instagram":"ronaldboersen","artaxis":null,"paypal